  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nThe Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry Chronicle 1949\n£10.00\n\nLow stock, 1 remaining\nThe Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry Chronicle 1949 quantity\nAdd to Cart\n\nCompiled and Edited by Brigadier-General C. G. Higgins, C.M.G., D.S.O. Volume LI January to December 1949.\n\nPublished 1950 - Slatter & Rose Oxford. Hardcover.\n\n \n\nContents:\n\nThe Army List\n\nExtracts from the London Gazette\n\nRecords of the First Battalion\n\nSummary of the First Battalion Diary\n\nFirst Battalion Letter\n\nCricket, First Battalion\n\nHockey, First Battalion\n\nFootball, First Battalion\n\nBoxing, First Battalion\n\nWeapon Training, First Battalion\n\nSignalling, First Battalion\n\nAthletics, First Battalion\n\nRecords of Regimental Headquarters\n\nHeadquarters Letter\n\nRecords of the Fourth Battalion\n\nFourth Battalion Letter\n\nThe Man with the Whistle\n\nRegimental Adjutant\n\nRegimental Dinner\n\nRegimental Luncheon\n\nThe 52nd Light Infantry Luncheon\n\nSickle Force\n\nEngland to Salonika 'En Famille'\n\nTrials of an Unmarried Husband\n\nShooting in Greece\n\nSouthern Rhodesia\n\nClose-Up of the 52nd at Waterloo\n\n'Forty Years On' - And More\n\nThe New Royal Military Academy, Sandhurst\n\nRandom Notes on the King's African Rifles\n\n'Oxi' Day\n\nA Record Nile Perch\n\nOperation Monkey\n\nRegimental Cricket Week\n\nThose Were The Days\n\nOld Comrades Association\n\nObituary\n\nIndex for Volumes XLII to LI\n\nPlease Note: Original copies supplied, all in used but reasonable condition. Copy supplied may vary slightly from the one pictured in terms of wear and aging.\n\n \n\nRelated products\nWinston Churchill: Oxfordshire Hussar – A Bugle & Sabre Special\n£2.00 Add to cart\nMESOPOTAMIA 1914-15: EXTRACTS FROM A REGIMENTAL OFFICER’S DIARY\n£11.99 Add to cart\nThe Story of the Oxfordshire Yeomanry – Queen’s Own Oxfordshire Hussars 1798-1998\n£7.95 Read more\nIdentifying Cap Badges: A Family Historian’s Guide\n£25.00 Add to cart\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
